MCP: 
MCPs follow a client-server architecture, agents use the MCP client to interact with an MCP server, so usually MCP clients are embedded within coding agents in IDEs like Cursor, Claude Code.
MCP server have 3 components: Resources for information, Tools for actions, and Prompts for reusable instructions

User
  ↓
AI Agent / Host
  ↓
MCP Client
  ↓
JSON-RPC messages
  ↓
MCP Server
  ↓
Tool / API / Database
  ↓
Result

MCP Client  ←── JSON-RPC ──→  MCP Server
    ↑                              ↓
   SDK                        Tools / Data


Build a MCP server:
1. import the FastMCP library and initialise a MCP server from it
2. define tools, resources and prompts
3. run the server and specify a transport protocol, either Standand IO or HTTP






